items.description:
I’m looking for a senior Product Designer / UI Designer / Art Director to redesign Stan from A to Z: product UI, website, design system and launch creatives.

Product

Stan is a browser extension for gamers browsing Steam.

Core experience:
Steam current price → Stan identifies the exact game/package/market → if a fresh, genuinely comparable external Steam-key offer qualifies, Stan can show it directly on Steam.

If no eligible offer exists, Stan stays discreet and shows nothing.

Stan is about current price comparison only. No price history, charts, predictions, “best time to buy”, fake crossed-out prices, “always cheaper” or “best price guaranteed”.

Some legacy materials still reflect an older price-history positioning. That direction is obsolete.

Existing product / access

* Website: stan-key.com
* Chrome extension: official Chrome Web Store listing — ID ehhomikpbeokopccgmienllpnambnkif
* Apple/Safari TestFlight: private link provided

Stan already works: audit the current UX/UI, challenge it and create a stronger unified system.

Scope — all user-facing surfaces

Browser extension

* Stan trigger beside eligible Steam purchase blocks;
* comparison drawer/modal;
* Steam Wishlist integration;
* first-run/onboarding;
* extension popup;
* merchant settings;
* sharing/QR + Steam tutorial;
* loading, unavailable, error and edge states.

It must integrate naturally into Steam while remaining clearly Stan and never implying Valve affiliation.

Apple / Safari
Redesign the SwiftUI host app for iPhone, iPad and macOS: Safari activation/readiness, setup, troubleshooting, “Open Steam”, plus the Safari popover.

It should feel native, not like a web popup inside an app.

Website
Redesign the public web system: homepage, product explanation, game/SEO pages, install/handoff states, key legal/privacy surfaces, responsive mobile UX and conversion flows.

Brand & Design System

The existing logo geometry remains unchanged.

Current DNA can evolve:

* black / white / grey;
* Stan orange used selectively;
* Inter / Inter Display where appropriate;
* minimal, precise, premium, modern tech;
* real product UI rather than fake dashboards.

Create a Figma system covering tokens, typography, spacing, grids, components, states and platform-specific patterns.

Stan supports 31 languages including Arabic RTL: layouts must handle localization, long strings and accessibility.

Brand qualities: simplicity, precision, trust, speed, immediate utility.

Avoid coupon/cashback/flash-sale aesthetics and exaggerated discount language.

Marketing system

After the product direction is established, create a few strong master concepts adaptable to:

* Apple App Store / Safari;
* Chrome, Firefox and Edge stores;
* Meta, Google PMax/Display, Reddit, X, ChatGPT Ads;
* editorial/sponsored content, press, OG/hero;
* display banners;
* short motion (~6s and 10–15s).

Core ratios: 1:1, 4:5, 9:16, 16:9 / ~1.91:1.

Create a reusable product screenshot library for stores, web, ads and press.

Deliverables

* UX/UI audit + creative direction;
* redesign of all user-facing product surfaces;
* website redesign;
* scalable Figma design system;
* interaction prototypes + key states;
* master marketing concepts + adaptations;
* store assets, screenshot library and motion;
* editable sources/exports;
* implementation-ready specs/tokens for developer handoff.

Private admin/back-office is out of scope unless agreed separately.

I prefer a few exceptional concepts and a rigorous system over many disconnected screens.

Please share relevant full-product redesigns, browser extensions, native/mobile apps and design systems. Mention collaborators used for specialist work.

Skills: Branding, Product Design, Prototyping, Figma, Visual Design, User Experience Research, Web Design, SwiftUI
